hey everyone I'm Abbi sharp welcome to  Abby's kitchen we've made it through the  indulgent holidays and bikini season  will be here before we know it but why  wait until summer to enjoy a nice crisp  cold beer now I know what you're  thinking we have New Year's resolutions  to uphold but I say all the more reason  to indulge the BeerBelly myth is so 2014  based more on the kinds of foods we  associate even with fear like nachos  potato chips pizza than anything  inherent about beer itself in reality  beer is low in sugar it's made with all  natural ingredients and ounce for ounce  it actually has fewer calories than wine  or spirits meaning if you sip and savor  you can mindly enjoy less also I bet you  didn't know that consuming one to two  beers a day has been linked to a reduced  risk of weight gain and heart disease  the key however is to enjoy it regularly  and not abstain all week long and then  binge on Saturday night and of course to  skip the bar food and favorite more  balanced meals  case in point my Brussels sprout and  apricot slaw with beer pesto vinaigrette  using beer in my salad dressings lets me  cut back on fat without compromising  flavor you're gonna love the result  first I shred a few cups of Brussels  sprouts fennel and apple and mix them  together with some finely diced dried  apricots then into my food processor I  grind my blanched whole almonds and  Parmesan cheese  then add in my parsley almond oil honey  lemon juice thyme leaves salt and pepper  and of course my favorite beer as a  simple rule of thumb loggers tend to go  best with sweet light greens pilsners  with peppery greens wheat beers with  fruity flavors and English ales with  earthy veggies and grains I'm using a  triple which works really well with  those cruciferous vegetables creamy  dressings and stone fruit when ready to  serve I toss the greens in the pesto and  garnish with toasted sliced almonds and  shaped Parmesan cheese  whoever said you can't make friends with  salad head never put a little beer on  top mindfully enjoying your favorite  beer with this Brussels sprout and a  profs law is total proof that getting  back on track before summer doesn't have  to suck thanks so much for watching guys  for great healthy recipes be sure to  subscribe to my channel and I'll see you  next time Abbey's kitchen
 

